[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（英音）]
[ti:Red for Danger]
[00:13.46]How was the drunk removed from the ring?
[00:19.86]During a bullfight, a drunk suddenly wandered into the middle of the ring.
[00:26.64]The crowd began to shout,
[00:29.47]but the drunk was unaware of the danger.
[00:33.83]The bull was busy with the matador at the time,
[00:37.65]but it suddenly caught sight of the drunk who was shouting rude remarks and waving a red cap.
[00:46.84]Apparently sensitive to criticism,
[00:50.32]the bull forgot all about the matador and charged at the drunk.
[00:57.03]The crowd suddenly grew quiet.
[01:00.76]The drunk, however, seemed quite sure of himself.
[01:05.46]When the bull got close to him,
[01:07.97]he clumsily stepped aside to let it pass.
[01:12.75]The crowd broke into cheers and the drunk bowed.
[01:18.97]By this time, however three men had come into the ring and they quickly dragged the drunk to safety.
[01:28.02]Even the bull seemed to feel sorry for him,
[01:31.40]for it looked on sympathetically until the drunk was out of the way before once more turning its attention to the matador.
